1
00:00:00,098 --> 00:00:02,707
we can go to the client index.html,

2
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:07,035
which is served by that same server for this

3
00:00:08,022 --> 00:00:08,572
/root route.

4
00:00:10,514 --> 00:00:12,658
And to show this in action, I can simply run

5
00:00:12,771 --> 00:00:15,318
bun run dev to start that server, which does

6
00:00:15,350 --> 00:00:17,446
start the server that handles the WebSockets

7
00:00:17,591 --> 00:00:19,234
and serves that root route

8
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:21,738
under localhost:3000.

9
00:00:23,238 --> 00:00:25,109
And if I open that, I see this chat window.

10
00:00:25,189 --> 00:00:27,173
Now here I can choose any name I want, any

11
00:00:27,269 --> 00:00:28,662
room name I want, And

12
00:00:29,884 --> 00:00:31,540
you see now I get some output here,

13
00:00:31,733 --> 00:00:34,210
connected to room general as Max and then

14
00:00:34,243 --> 00:00:35,722
Max joined general.

15
00:00:36,540 --> 00:00:37,766
Where is this coming from?

16
00:00:38,508 --> 00:00:40,992
Well, as mentioned, we're serving the

17
00:00:40,992 --> 00:00:44,154
homepage here. So this is this index.html

18
00:00:44,154 --> 00:00:44,558
file.

19
00:00:45,917 --> 00:00:48,312
And in that file I got of course the HTML

20
00:00:48,425 --> 00:00:51,046
and the styling or the imported styles for

21
00:00:51,046 --> 00:00:51,450
the look,

22
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,748
but then I got client.ts.

23
00:00:54,828 --> 00:00:56,960
So I'm importing a TypeScript file here and

24
00:00:57,040 --> 00:00:59,686
that will be compiled by Bun because we have

25
00:00:59,686 --> 00:01:02,812
it in an HTML file that is imported by a

26
00:01:02,828 --> 00:01:05,072
Bun-executed file. You learned about that

27
00:01:05,072 --> 00:01:07,284
earlier in the course that Bun would then

28
00:01:07,381 --> 00:01:09,288
handle the compilation of these files.

29
00:01:09,962 --> 00:01:11,533
So that's what's happening here. But what is

30
00:01:11,629 --> 00:01:13,120
in that client.ts file?

31
00:01:13,649 --> 00:01:14,563
Well, in there

32
00:01:15,156 --> 00:01:17,849
I have some vanilla TypeScript for handling

33
00:01:17,897 --> 00:01:20,141
and updating the UI. So I reach out to a

34
00:01:20,206 --> 00:01:22,562
bunch of HTML elements in there to be able

35
00:01:22,562 --> 00:01:24,630
to interact with them and listen to clicks

36
00:01:24,630 --> 00:01:24,999
and so on.

37
00:01:25,673 --> 00:01:29,594
But what's important in here is that in the

38
00:01:29,610 --> 00:01:29,948
end,

39
00:01:30,478 --> 00:01:32,390
I have this listener

40
00:01:32,969 --> 00:01:35,207
for the submission of the connect form,

41
00:01:37,164 --> 00:01:39,945
which is just this form here at the top. So

42
00:01:39,945 --> 00:01:41,934
not the form where I send a message, but

43
00:01:41,934 --> 00:01:43,179
this form where I connect it.

44
00:01:43,728 --> 00:01:45,638
I have a listener to the submission of that

45
00:01:45,654 --> 00:01:48,664
form and in there I have the client side for

46
00:01:48,664 --> 00:01:50,185
connecting to the WebSocket server.

47
00:01:50,760 --> 00:01:53,711
So here I'm in the end defining a URL I

48
00:01:53,711 --> 00:01:54,343
wanna connect to and in the end here that

49
00:01:54,343 --> 00:01:55,251
will just be the URL of the server

50
00:01:57,813 --> 00:02:00,762
that is serving this site, but the protocol

51
00:02:01,082 --> 00:02:04,721
will be WS or if it were deployed, WSS for

52
00:02:04,721 --> 00:02:06,836
the secure version of it, which means

53
00:02:07,093 --> 00:02:10,122
WebSocket instead of HTTP or HTTPS.

54
00:02:11,116 --> 00:02:12,478
But then we target the

55
00:02:13,023 --> 00:02:15,348
/chat route, which is in line with what we

56
00:02:15,380 --> 00:02:18,457
expect on the server and we pass our room

57
00:02:18,954 --> 00:02:21,599
and our name as query parameters to that

58
00:02:21,599 --> 00:02:24,179
URL, which again is also in line with what

59
00:02:24,179 --> 00:02:25,397
we extract on the server.

60
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:29,456
So that's how we send this, hey, I wanna

61
00:02:29,456 --> 00:02:31,814
connect request from the client to the

62
00:02:31,814 --> 00:02:34,204
server. And then on the client, so in the

63
00:02:34,204 --> 00:02:37,028
browser, we instantiate a WebSocket object.

64
00:02:37,172 --> 00:02:39,257
And this is now not Bun, this is a browser

65
00:02:39,257 --> 00:02:42,450
API. We instantiate a WebSocket object and

66
00:02:42,466 --> 00:02:45,450
we add a listener to open events that may be

67
00:02:45,450 --> 00:02:48,000
sent by that WebSocket connection. So by

68
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,663
instantiating this with the URL, we're

69
00:02:50,663 --> 00:02:54,014
sending a request to the backend. So we send

70
00:02:54,014 --> 00:02:56,305
the request that will be handled by the BUN

71
00:02:56,353 --> 00:02:59,429
server and there the BUN server will upgrade

72
00:02:59,461 --> 00:03:01,528
the connection to a WebSocket connection and

73
00:03:01,689 --> 00:03:03,964
that's how this connection is established

74
00:03:04,092 --> 00:03:05,935
from both the server and client side. And

75
00:03:05,951 --> 00:03:08,482
then here we listen to the open event which

76
00:03:08,658 --> 00:03:10,661
will be triggered automatically once the

77
00:03:10,661 --> 00:03:12,904
connection was established by both server

78
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:15,051
and client. So just as we have an open

79
00:03:15,388 --> 00:03:17,791
method here on the server for confirming it,

80
00:03:18,047 --> 00:03:20,210
we have an event to which we can listen on

81
00:03:20,210 --> 00:03:20,787
the client.

82
00:03:21,333 --> 00:03:23,659
And it's here where I in the end update my

83
00:03:23,723 --> 00:03:26,066
UI to say connected to room blah, blah,

84
00:03:26,082 --> 00:03:26,307
blah.

85
00:03:26,852 --> 00:03:29,275
That is this message you see here. But this

86
00:03:29,275 --> 00:03:31,345
message below is coming from the server.

87
00:03:31,763 --> 00:03:34,346
This message is sent or published by the

88
00:03:34,346 --> 00:03:37,218
server when the connection is confirmed by

89
00:03:37,282 --> 00:03:38,678
the server in its open method.

90
00:03:39,288 --> 00:03:42,642
Here we send this joined room message

91
00:03:43,236 --> 00:03:45,273
and on the client we react to that by adding

92
00:03:45,322 --> 00:03:47,696
another event listener for messages sent by

93
00:03:47,728 --> 00:03:50,135
the server. So messages published by the

94
00:03:50,135 --> 00:03:52,109
server. So whenever the server calls

95
00:03:52,270 --> 00:03:54,631
publish, this triggers this message event

96
00:03:54,631 --> 00:03:56,317
listener to become active on the client.

97
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:58,887
And here we then extract some data, and

98
00:03:58,887 --> 00:04:00,381
therefore of course we need to know which

99
00:04:00,494 --> 00:04:02,437
kind of data the server sends because I

100
00:04:02,485 --> 00:04:04,236
mentioned that the shape of this data is

101
00:04:04,268 --> 00:04:06,453
totally up to you. So as a developer, you

102
00:04:06,453 --> 00:04:08,204
have to make sure that on the client side

103
00:04:08,204 --> 00:04:10,099
you're working with the same kind of data as

104
00:04:10,212 --> 00:04:10,870
on the backend.

105
00:04:11,641 --> 00:04:13,713
But we parse the message here that was sent

106
00:04:13,745 --> 00:04:15,448
by the server, that was published by the

107
00:04:15,448 --> 00:04:15,833
server.

108
00:04:16,540 --> 00:04:18,803
I check the message type but I only do that

109
00:04:18,803 --> 00:04:21,112
in the end for styling purposes because that

110
00:04:21,112 --> 00:04:23,452
all then is client-side logic for adding and

111
00:04:23,452 --> 00:04:25,231
displaying a message in a certain style.

112
00:04:25,921 --> 00:04:28,485
And I simply show messages differently based

113
00:04:28,485 --> 00:04:30,281
on whether they were sent by the system or

114
00:04:30,281 --> 00:04:30,906
some user.

115
00:04:31,611 --> 00:04:33,679
And that is then how the message text is

116
00:04:33,791 --> 00:04:34,433
displayed there.

117
00:04:34,994 --> 00:04:36,581
And then on the client side, I also have

118
00:04:36,597 --> 00:04:39,145
logic for the connection being closed where

119
00:04:39,145 --> 00:04:41,742
I say disconnected from the server and so

120
00:04:41,871 --> 00:04:42,015
on.

121
00:04:42,848 --> 00:04:44,980
But now on the server, I have more methods,

122
00:04:45,029 --> 00:04:47,257
not just open. I also have a message and a

123
00:04:47,257 --> 00:04:49,709
close method as I mentioned and messages

124
00:04:49,790 --> 00:04:52,035
triggered whenever a client sends a message

125
00:04:52,227 --> 00:04:53,799
because in client.ts,

126
00:04:54,376 --> 00:04:56,733
I also have this message form where I listen

127
00:04:56,781 --> 00:04:57,647
for submit events.

128
00:04:58,465 --> 00:05:01,336
And that is that other form on this screen,

129
00:05:01,688 --> 00:05:04,030
which is this form down here when a user

130
00:05:04,030 --> 00:05:07,045
sends a message. So I can send hi there and

131
00:05:07,045 --> 00:05:09,691
if I click send or hit enter, you see that

132
00:05:09,691 --> 00:05:10,300
shows up here.

133
00:05:10,829 --> 00:05:13,154
And it shows up here because when I submit

134
00:05:13,154 --> 00:05:15,849
that form on the client, what's happening is

135
00:05:16,346 --> 00:05:19,973
I'm sending that message to my WebSocket

136
00:05:19,973 --> 00:05:21,577
connection. So again, this is the

137
00:05:21,577 --> 00:05:24,049
client-side JavaScript code. We established

138
00:05:24,049 --> 00:05:26,777
a WebSocket connection here, we got a socket

139
00:05:26,857 --> 00:05:29,778
handle as a result, and we can use that for

140
00:05:29,842 --> 00:05:32,072
communicating with the server. And that's

141
00:05:32,072 --> 00:05:33,629
what's happening here. We're sending a

142
00:05:33,629 --> 00:05:34,817
message to the server.

143
00:05:35,459 --> 00:05:38,122
And on the server, that triggers the message

144
00:05:38,283 --> 00:05:40,064
event handler here, as you could say.

145
00:05:40,594 --> 00:05:42,600
We get the message as an input here and we

146
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:45,232
then publish it. We publish it to send it to

147
00:05:45,472 --> 00:05:46,467
all connected

148
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:49,200
clients, because of course the idea is that

149
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:51,921
multiple clients can connect. I can open

150
00:05:51,921 --> 00:05:54,078
this browser window again. So now I have 2,

151
00:05:54,561 --> 00:05:57,139
1 and 2, and in the second one I can connect

152
00:05:57,139 --> 00:05:57,770
as Andy

153
00:05:59,823 --> 00:06:01,554
to the same room. That's important, same

154
00:06:01,602 --> 00:06:04,109
identifier, because that is the topic to

155
00:06:04,109 --> 00:06:05,370
which messages are published.

156
00:06:05,952 --> 00:06:08,498
So now Andy joined on the first window. I

157
00:06:08,547 --> 00:06:11,092
can see that Andy joined because again,

158
00:06:11,204 --> 00:06:14,180
they're connected through WebSockets to the

159
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:17,146
same server and subscribed to the same

160
00:06:17,274 --> 00:06:19,550
topic. That's how messages are shared.

161
00:06:20,256 --> 00:06:22,019
And now if I send a new message from Max

162
00:06:22,019 --> 00:06:22,131
here,

163
00:06:23,622 --> 00:06:24,696
hi Max again,

164
00:06:25,465 --> 00:06:27,934
I see it here in that window, but I also see

165
00:06:27,934 --> 00:06:30,034
it in that other window, but they are sent

166
00:06:30,034 --> 00:06:30,852
from another user.

167
00:06:31,717 --> 00:06:33,993
And if I now send, hi, I'm Andy here,

168
00:06:35,308 --> 00:06:36,398
you see it shows up here,

169
00:06:36,991 --> 00:06:39,251
but of course also for Max, but here sent

170
00:06:39,251 --> 00:06:41,768
from another window. So that's how these 2

171
00:06:42,057 --> 00:06:44,702
clients, these 2 separate sessions connect

172
00:06:44,782 --> 00:06:47,110
to the same server and subscribed to the

173
00:06:47,110 --> 00:06:50,434
same topic. That is how this works. And this

174
00:06:50,466 --> 00:06:52,939
message handler on the server needs to

175
00:06:52,971 --> 00:06:55,508
publish messages sent by the client so that

176
00:06:55,540 --> 00:06:58,623
one topic for all clients shows the same

177
00:06:58,671 --> 00:07:01,128
messages or receives the same messages.

178
00:07:02,589 --> 00:07:03,825
And now if I

179
00:07:04,676 --> 00:07:05,977
close this window here,

180
00:07:06,683 --> 00:07:08,369
I of course only have Max.

181
00:07:10,553 --> 00:07:13,220
If I connect again with some user, I see

182
00:07:13,220 --> 00:07:15,131
that user. And if Max should click

183
00:07:15,131 --> 00:07:15,886
disconnect here,

184
00:07:16,963 --> 00:07:19,308
I also see that there. And sorry, that was

185
00:07:19,308 --> 00:07:21,959
Andy, not Max. So I see that here too. And

186
00:07:21,959 --> 00:07:23,501
of course we could also try listening to

187
00:07:23,501 --> 00:07:25,814
events when the browser closes so that we

188
00:07:25,814 --> 00:07:28,786
then also leave the server. Otherwise we'll

189
00:07:28,786 --> 00:07:30,457
leave automatically after a certain

190
00:07:30,457 --> 00:07:32,786
timeframe. But that is in a nutshell how you

191
00:07:32,802 --> 00:07:35,919
can set up a WebSocket server and also a

192
00:07:35,919 --> 00:07:38,087
client with help of Bun. Though for the

193
00:07:38,087 --> 00:07:39,998
client, it's really worth noting that in

194
00:07:40,030 --> 00:07:41,347
this browser example here,

195
00:07:41,957 --> 00:07:44,734
we're using the browser WebSocket support.

196
00:07:44,847 --> 00:07:47,625
This is not BUN, but for the server it of

197
00:07:47,641 --> 00:07:48,026
course is.
